      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "Saying \"my\", \"your\", \"his\" with 的",
      "body": "To show that something belongs to someone, put 的 after the person: 我的 means \"my\", 你的 means \"your\", 他的 means \"his\". It works like \"'s\" in English. With family members and other close relationships, 的 is usually left out, so \"my mom\" is simply 我妈妈.",
